vine 1.2.0
title: Durable Scrivener - Journal Contract to Distributed Semantics
prefix: scriv
---
[durable-scrivener] Durable Scrivener (planning)
Lift IScrivener from an implicit in-memory contract to a formalized journal contract with a durable single-node implementation and a path to distributed semantics. Geas Arcana invariant #1 (re-derivability: world state reconstructs from journal alone) is the driving consumer; Coven audit found the current contract is only true of InMemoryScrivener.
-> contract
-> contract-tests
-> segment-log
-> hydration
-> cursors
-> dedup
-> retire-filescrivener
-> sequencer
-> replication
-> geas-integration
> Contract before code: every guarantee gets written down and enforced by a shared test suite before any new implementation lands
> Multi-match fan-out (Tee dispatch) is a hard requirement; every consumer owns an independent cursor - fan-out is never designed away
> Delivery model: at-least-once plus idempotent effects, not exactly-once transport
